---
import './Trust.css';
---

<section class="trust dark-field" id="controls" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
  <div class="trust-inner">
    <header class="trust-intro">
      <div>
        <p>Configured by your operation</p>
        <h2 id="trust-title">Your rules are the product boundary.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Austi should know what it may do, when it must pause and the precise moment a person needs to take over.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="control-boundary">
      <ol class="boundary-rules" aria-label="Austi operating boundary">
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>01 · Within policy</span>
          <h3>Coordinate.</h3>
          <p>When the evidence is clear and the work sits inside the configured limit, Austi can prepare the preferred contractor and keep everyone updated.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>02 · Boundary reached</span>
          <h3>Pause.</h3>
          <p>When cost, responsibility or authority is unclear, the case stops at the exact decision instead of silently moving forward.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>03 · Judgment required</span>
          <h3>Hand over.</h3>
          <p>Danger, conflicting evidence, sensitive context or a request for a person goes straight to the responsible manager with the case prepared.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <aside class="approval-example" aria-labelledby="approval-example-title">
        <p class="approval-example-kicker">Case 024 · Kitchen leak</p>
        <h3 id="approval-example-title">Quote above owner limit.</h3>
        <p>The preferred plumber is ready for tomorrow at 09:00. Austi pauses before booking.</p>
        <footer>
          <span>Manager decision</span>
          <strong>Approve or hold.</strong>
        </footer>
      </aside>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
